@startuml status-line-context-gauge
!include _standard-style.puml

title Context Window Gauge — one implementation, four agents

top to bottom direction

' NOTE ON LABELS: PlantUML creole treats "~" as an escape and a leading "*" as a
' bullet, so "~/.copilot" renders as "/.copilot" and "*.jsonl" becomes a list
' item. Paths below use $HOME and a named placeholder instead of relying on
' escaping — it survives edits better than a stray "~~".

rectangle "Pane identity — exported per session by tmux-session-wrapper.sh" {
  component "CODING_AGENT\nTRANSCRIPT_SOURCE_PROJECT\nTMUX_SESSION_NAME" as PaneEnv <<infra>>
}

rectangle "Per-agent context sources" {
  database "claude\n$TMPDIR/claude-ctx-<id>.json\nremaining_percentage" as ClaudeBridge <<storage>>
  database "opencode\nopencode.db message.tokens\ninput + cache.read" as OpencodeDb <<storage>>
  database "copilot\n$HOME/.copilot/session-store.db\ninput_tokens ONLY" as CopilotDb <<storage>>
  database "pi\n<piCfgDir>/sessions/<file>.jsonl\ninput + cacheRead" as PiSessions <<storage>>
}

component "lib/statusline/context-gauge.cjs" as Gauge <<core>>

rectangle "Renderers" {
  component "combined-status-line.js\nfull render (ESM)" as CSL <<core>>
  database "cache-<project>-<agent>-w<width>.txt" as Cache <<storage>>
  component "status-line-fast.cjs\n5s tick (CJS)" as Fast <<core>>
}

component "tmux status-right" as Tmux <<external>>

PaneEnv CONTROL_LINE Gauge : which reader,\nwhich project
ClaudeBridge DATA_LINE Gauge
OpencodeDb DATA_LINE Gauge
CopilotDb DATA_LINE Gauge
PiSessions DATA_LINE Gauge

Gauge SYNC_LINE CSL : render into the line
CSL DATA_LINE Cache : write
Cache DATA_LINE Fast : read
Gauge SYNC_LINE Fast : re-render in place
Fast SYNC_LINE Tmux

' The two-wires warning is a LEGEND rather than a note anchored to CopilotDb:
' a note on a node inside a rectangle gets placed outside that rectangle, and
' PlantUML then draws a connector clear across the top of the diagram to reach
' it. The content is about the picture as a whole anyway.
legend bottom
  <b>The two wires disagree — this is where that bites.</b>
  Copilot is OpenAI wire: input_tokens ALREADY includes cache reads.
  OpenCode and pi are Anthropic wire, where cache reads add.
  Adding them on the copilot path would roughly double a cache-heavy
  reading, and nothing would error.
endlegend

note right of Gauge
  CommonJS so BOTH renderers load the
  same file — no second copy to keep
  in step.

  Returns null, never 0%, when a store
  cannot be read: an empty gauge and a
  blind one must not look alike.

  Fixed 15 cells in every severity
  band, measured against tmux. Width
  drift here is the trailing-residue
  bug.
end note

note right of Fast
  Patches the gauge in place so the
  number stays live between full
  renders. A line borrowed from a
  sibling pane is BLANKED first —
  same width, no reading — because
  that value is another session's.
end note

@enduml
